---
title: Ink, XP, and respec
pageSlug: ink-and-xp
mod: spell-codex
section: gameplay
order: 3
---

Each next tier wants **XP** and **one ink** of the matching rarity. Common ink will not unlock a legendary rank. The ink slots under the Codex are the filter: select a rarity and the **+** buttons that do not match go dull.

Hold a focus for that school and the XP cost drops by **25%**. Ink cost does not. Creative mode skips the ink, which is handy when you are testing a pack.

**Respec** gives back a slice of spent XP. Default is 25%, and pack authors can change that in `codex_settings.json`. You cannot respec a spell you never paid for.

If you just want more spells in the book without hunting rares, make an **Empty Codex Page** (paper + any Iron’s ink at an Arcane Anvil) and imprint at the **Scroll Forge** with a school focus. That costs 10 levels and only rolls undiscovered spells whose tier-1 ink is at or under the page’s rarity. It is the “I would rather craft than loot” path.

Authors who want to hide a spell or lock a whole school can do it in JSON under `config/specs_irons_spellbooks/`. `spell_blacklist.json` and `school_access.json` are the two people actually touch. `/specs_codex school lock` is the live version of that for ops.
